  "faqs": [
    {
      "q": "Can I buy from the Lux Store today?",
      "a": "The Store is live for browsing, comparing and saving items. Payment, final pricing and fulfillment remain disabled until those commercial systems are commissioned."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does adding something to the bag charge me?",
      "a": "No. The current bag is a prelaunch saved-items list. It never collects payment information and does not place an order."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Lux Verify PASS mean on a Store item?",
      "a": "For new Kit Creator public releases, it means the required quality and verification fields and evidence passed the Store publishing gate. It is not a promise that every external service or future environment will behave identically."
    },
    {
      "q": "Why do the older Prompt Kits say legacy approved listing?",
      "a": "They were already approved Store products before the newer contract-v2 publishing gate existed. They are not being relabeled as having passed a test they did not run."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I get help with an installed Lux product?",
      "a": "Use the Help & Legal or support area inside Lux Agent Desktop so guidance can match the edition and setup you are actually running."
    },
    {
      "q": "Will devices have exact storage, speed and compatibility specs here?",
      "a": "Yes, but only after the customer SKU and fulfillment configuration are locked. The Store avoids inventing hardware specifications before that point."
    },
    {
      "q": "How are new Prompt Kits published?",
      "a": "Lux Codex Kit Creator prepares the pack and its release assets. New public contract-v2 packs must clear the quality and Lux Verify publishing gate before the Store sync can publish them."
    },
    {
      "q": "Is Lux Codex a customer product?",
      "a": "Lux Codex is the private founder control plane for operating the Lux business and Store. Customers use Lux Agent Desktop and the customer-facing Lux ecosystem."
    }
